---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Math for AI, at a glance
summary: Every idea from the calculus series on one page, with its formula, the idea in a sentence, where it shows up in a neural network, and its hidden meaning, which is what it says about how a network learns.
permalink: /math/cheat-sheet/
---
{#- The quick-look cheat sheet. Content lives in _data/cheatsheet.yaml. -#}
<article class="cheat">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/math/">Math</a><span class="sep">/</span>Cheat sheet</p>
    <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
    <p class="dek">{{ summary }}</p>
    <p class="resource-links">
      <a class="pill" href="/assets/pdf/math-for-ai-cheat-sheet.pdf" download>Download this as a PDF</a>
      <a class="pill" href="/assets/pdf/calculus-for-ai.pdf" download>Full series PDF</a>
      <a class="pill" href="/math/calculus-for-ai/">Read the series</a>
    </p>
    <p class="print-only cheat-source">{{ site.author }} · {{ page.url | absUrl }} · {{ builtAt | month }}</p>
  </header>

  {%- for section in cheatsheet.sections %}
  <section class="cheat-section">
    <h2 class="section-label">{{ section.title }}</h2>
    <div class="cheat-grid">
      {%- for item in section.items %}
      <article class="cheat-card">
        <h3><a href="/notebook/{{ item.part }}/">{{ item.concept }}</a></h3>
        <div class="cheat-formula">{{ item.tex | tex(true) | safe }}</div>
        <p><span class="label">Idea</span>{{ item.idea | mathText | safe }}</p>
        <p><span class="label">In AI</span>{{ item.ai | mathText | safe }}</p>
        {%- if item.meaning %}
        <p class="cheat-meaning"><span class="label">Hidden meaning</span>{{ item.meaning | mathText | safe }}</p>
        {%- endif %}
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}

  {%- set n = cheatsheet.neuron %}
  <section class="cheat-section">
    <h2 class="section-label">One neuron, by hand</h2>
    <div class="cheat-grid">
      <article class="cheat-card">
        <h3><a href="/notebook/partial-derivatives-and-one-neuron/">Forward pass</a></h3>
        <div class="cheat-formula">{{ n.setup | tex(true) | safe }}</div>
        <table class="cheat-table">
          {%- for row in n.forward %}
          <tr><td>{{ row[0] | tex | safe }}</td><td>{{ row[1] | tex | safe }}</td></tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </table>
      </article>
      <article class="cheat-card">
        <h3><a href="/notebook/the-gradient/">Backward pass, then one step</a></h3>
        <table class="cheat-table">
          {%- for row in n.backward %}
          <tr><td>{{ row[0] | tex | safe }}</td><td>{{ row[1] | tex | safe }}</td></tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </table>
        <p class="cheat-ai"><span class="label">Step</span>{{ n.step | mathText | safe }}</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cheat-section">
    <h2 class="section-label">Easy slips</h2>
    <ul class="cheat-slips">
      {%- for slip in cheatsheet.slips %}
      <li>{{ slip | mathText | safe }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <footer class="entry-foot">
    <p>Each card links to the part that derives it. <a href="/notebook/the-hidden-meaning-of-the-calculus/">Read the hidden meanings as one story →</a></p>
    <p><a href="/math/calculus-for-ai/">Start the series from the beginning →</a></p>
  </footer>
</article>
